(Stage 1e3 - nothing rides in a mixed list slot (tag 6) and prints in
 place; a later `is nothing` test on that slot classifies it by its
 stored tag, while a non-nothing slot does not. Acceptance: the print
 line and the two predicate lines.)

a list called "xs" is [1, nothing, 2].
print xs.
if element 2 of xs is nothing, print "element 2 is nothing".
if element 1 of xs is not nothing, print "element 1 is not nothing".